<title>ISRAEL: Northrop Grumman to buy Tadiran batteries.</title>
<headline>Northrop Grumman to buy Tadiran batteries.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tadiran Ltd said Tuesday that it received an initial $250,000 order from Northrop Grumman Corp. for lithium batteries to power cordless modems.</p>
<p>The Israeli electronics firm added that its batteries unit expected to receive additional orders from the U.S. defence company totalling some $2.5 million.</p>
<p>Tadiran said the lightweight, high-energy battery had been under development for the past seven years.</p>
</text>
